type Section = { title: string; content: ReactNode };
function BriefView({ title, sections }: { title: string; sections: Section[] }) {
  return (
    <article>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      {sections.map(s => <Section key={s.title} title={s.title}>{s.content}</Section>)}
    </article>
  );
}
```
This differs from the earlier config-driven guess because the shape — an outer shell plus a list of labeled sections — was verified against three real, different brief types, not assumed from one. The parts that turned out to be genuinely shared (the article wrapper, the title) are hardcoded; the part that turned out to genuinely vary (the sections) is the actual parameter — both facts checked against evidence instead of guessed.

